aved polygon plus DRC results","Simulation models ideal lumped R and C per the stated scope; board parasitics, component tolerances, voltage/power ratings, loading and EMC were deliberately not assessed because inputs/requirements.txt restricts evaluation to the ideal unloaded step response and forbids imposing unstated requirements","The ideal step was approximated with a 1 ns PWL ramp in ngspice; the resulting error at t = 1 ms is far below 1 uV and does not affect the pass/fail determination"],"findings":[{"id":"CIR-01","title":"Packet check set contains no electrical measurement of the sole stated electrical requirement (independent simulation shows the circuit passes)","location":"packet criteria (erc/drc/netlist/geometry) vs inputs/requirements.txt","condition":"The only pass/fail requirement is electrical: /OUT must be 0.62-0.65 V at t = 1 ms after a 1 V step at /IN with the capacitor initially discharged. The supplied checks are ERC, DRC, netlist export and geometry extraction; none of them stimulates or measures the circuit, so a fully passing packet would not by itself demonstrate compliance.","mechanism":"ERC/DRC/netlist exit status proves rule and connectivity consistency, not transient behavior; a wrong R or C value (e.g. 1k or 10n) would produce an identical all-pass packet while failing the voltage window. Independent verification closes the gap: ngspice-42 transient on the exported netlist (R1=10k IN-OUT, C1=100n OUT-GND, 1 V step, IC=0, unloaded) gives v(OUT)=0.6321204 V at 1 ms, matching the analytic 1-e^-1 = 0.632121 V for tau = RC = 1.000 ms, inside the window with +12.1 mV / +17.9 mV margins.","severity":"info","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"inputs/requirements.txt","locator":"lines 1-2 (0.62-0.65 V at 1 ms requirement)"},{"path":"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch","locator":"symbol R1 Value \"10k\" (at 86.36 63.5); symbol C1 Value \"100n\" (at 101.6 63.5)"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"nets: /IN={J1.1,R1.1},